# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Frontend build-time defaults. COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
#  These are NOT secrets — Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the public
#  bundle, so anything here is visible to any user. Never put a credential in
#  this file.
#
#  It is committed so that every build has a DEFINITE value. That matters for
#  index.html, where `%VITE_API_ORIGIN%` is substituted at build time: if the
#  variable is undefined, Vite leaves the placeholder literal, and
#  `connect-src 'self' %VITE_API_ORIGIN%` is then an INVALID CSP source
#  expression — which can make the browser drop the whole directive.
#
#  Override per environment in `.env.local` (gitignored) or in the Cloudflare
#  Pages dashboard. Precedence: shell > .env.local > .env
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Absolute API URL INCLUDING /api/v1.
#   EMPTY = local development. The Vite dev server proxies /api to :8080, so the
#   browser sees one origin and CORS never applies locally.
#   Production: https://phc-api-xxxxx-ew.a.run.app/api/v1
VITE_API_URL=

# Origin ONLY (no path, no trailing slash) for the CSP connect-src.
#   Production: VITE_API_ORIGIN="https://phc-api-xxxxx-ew.a.run.app"
#
#   The default is "'self'" — a QUOTED LITERAL, which is valid CSP for local
#   development where the Vite proxy makes the API same-origin. It must not be
#   left blank: `connect-src 'self' ` with a dangling space is malformed, and a
#   malformed source list can make a browser discard the whole directive.
#
#   Keep the inner single quotes in the production value too, so the substituted
#   CSP stays well-formed:
#     VITE_API_ORIGIN="'self' https://phc-api-xxxxx-ew.a.run.app"
VITE_API_ORIGIN="'self'"
